# FX's four rows: REVERB 2 (MOTION, LOW CUT, INTERVAL: the shimmer an octave, a fifth or a twelfth up,
# LEVEL) and DELAY 2 (LEVEL, LOW CUT, PING-PONG, WARP's range). The throws: DIP both ways (left a low-pass
# closing, right a high-pass opening), WARP on ALGO (the delay's time bent), all drifting back. A scene's
# ROOM (the reverb's size and decay) and HALO (its shimmer) over the page's, gliding with PRESET: the
# lines slew, no click. Audio in fxmore.wav.
wait 500
tap FX
turn SELECT 1
expect fxrow 1
turn K3 1
expect fx10 1
shot fx_rows.png
turn SELECT 2
expect fxrow 3
turn K3 -1
expect fx14 0
turn K3 1
expect fx14 1
wav fxmore.wav
tapkey w2
wait 400
tapkey w4
press FX
turn K4 -20
wait 100
expect perf3 <-60
turn K4 40
wait 100
expect perf3 >60
turn ALGO -10
wait 100
expect perf9 <-50
shot throws.png
release FX
wait 3500
expect perf3 0
expect perf9 0
tap EDIT
turn SELECT 7
turn K2 20
expect room1 104
turn SELECT 1
turn K2 10
expect halo1 84
tapkey w5
turn PRESET 1
wait 13000
expect scene 2
tapkey w3
wait 3000
wavstop
expect clips 0
